About

    This subdirectory contains a patch that exposes AGAMA's Fortran interface to Ramses.

    IMPORTANT: The AGAMA library must be compiled on the SAME system that this patch is meant to be run!

    The directory 'devel' was used as a development space. It has been kept for future reference and guidance.

Usage

    Compile Ramses patch with either of:

        - Makefile_AGAMA_MULTIPATCH
        - Makefile_AGAMA_DICE_MULTIPATCH

    In the NML, include the following block:

    ! file path is set by initfile (in INIT_PARAMS):
    &AGAMA_PARAMS
    agama_file = 'some_agama_potential.ini'
    agama_debug = .true.       ! overrides agama_verbose
    agama_verbose = .true.     ! better to set to .true. (:default)
    agama_file = 0.0           ! controls the file read frequency (default: 1e10)
    /

    See Notes below.

Notes
    - agama_file is either an INI file with [Potential] section, either specifing an analytic potential or  with a potential approximation and derivatives (with its coefficients, etc.)
    - the file is read at every t_step; the default value of t_step = 1e10 means the file is only read at t = 0.


